<td id="S5.T4.2.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">34.2</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Post-training Strategies</span>: Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 5.4 Ablation Study ‣ 5 Results ‣ Stream RAG: Instant and Accurate SpokenDialogue Systems with Streaming Tool Usage" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> presents performance comparison under different post-training conditions. Incorporating streaming tool query generation during post-training (S. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS2" title="3.2.2 Model-Triggered Streaming RAG ‣ 3.2 Streaming RAG ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Stream RAG: Instant and Accurate SpokenDialogue Systems with Streaming Tool Usage" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.2</span></a>) results in comparable performance for both models. These results suggest that <em id="S5.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Model-Triggered Streaming RAG</em> can be integrated into post-training process without negatively impacting model performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Ablation Results for Negative Sampling Strategy in <em id="S5.T5.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Model-Triggered Streaming RAG</em> (S. <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS2" title="3.2.2 Model-Triggered Streaming RAG ‣ 3.2 Streaming RAG ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Stream RAG: Instant and Accurate SpokenDialogue Systems with Streaming Tool Usage" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.2</span></a>).</figcaption>
